  "paragraph": 14,
  "text": "Now move to Pillar Two: context management and cache economics. Think of the context window as the agent's RAM. Even when a frontier model advertises two hundred thousand or one million tokens of capacity, reasoning quality does not stay flat all the way to the wall. As giant stack traces, stale file reads, and abandoned attempts accumulate, signal gets buried in noise, a phenomenon engineers call context rot. Performance degrades long before the window is full, so deciding what enters and stays in context is a primary harness job.",
